32	+Runlog's plugin is in the Stream Deck Marketplace, under **Runlog**. Install it and eight actions appear in the action list: Connect, Run, Do the next thing, Press, Roll, Apply setup, Undo, and Metric. It needs the Stream Deck app at 7.1 or later.
33	 
34	 ## Signing in
35	 
36	 Every key's settings carry the same account block: the Runlog address, **Sign in**, **Sign out**, **Reconnect**, and a line saying who is signed in. Leave the address alone unless you run a copy of your own.
37	 
38	 **Sign in** shows a code and a link. Open the link in a browser, type the code, and you are signed in on the deck; the plugin keeps that sign-in in a file of its own, not in the settings the pages read. Signing in is not connecting: press Connect after.
39	 
40	 ## Connect
41	 
42	 **Connect** opens the connection, and pressing it again closes it. Nothing is open until you press it, and a connection holding no run closes itself after thirty minutes — the key then says _Idle · press to connect_. A deck that is following a run stays up however long the stream goes.
43	@@ -17,20 +17,21 @@ Every other key says **Not connected**, with _press Connect_ beneath it, while t
44	 ## The run the deck is on
45	 
46	 The deck presses through the page that holds the run, so it only ever sees a run that is synced to your account and open on a page somewhere: the app in a browser tab, a [dock](#guide/dock), or a browser source. With nothing synced the keys say **Not synced**; with runs synced but none open, **No run open**.
47	 
48	 **Run** names the run the deck is following. Press it to cycle through the runs open to you and pin the next one; its settings list the same runs by name. A pin holds: a pinned run that ends says **That run has ended** rather than moving the deck to whichever run went next. Where one run is open and nothing is pinned, the deck follows that one; where several are open and none is pinned, the keys say **Pick a run**.
49	 
50	 ## The keys
51	 
52	 - **Do the next thing** presses whatever the run is waiting on — rolling the table, carrying on, closing the unit, entering the next — and carries the step's own words. Where the step waits on a checklist it ticks everything and presses the step's own button; where it waits on a name, it takes the first suggestion. Tick **Stop at decisions** in its settings and it leaves both to the page.
53	 - **Press** does the one thing you pick in its settings: a move the pack offers, the roll that is waiting, or a preset answer.
54	+- **Roll** throws the dice the run is waiting on. It needs no settings, and is lit only while a roll is on offer.
55	 - **Apply setup** changes the run's loadout to a setup from your library and hands it out to the tool, set in its settings. The list is your library for the pack's tool; a tool has to be attached to the run for the hand-out to reach it.
56	 - **Undo** takes back the last result. It is lit when there is something to take back and dim when there is not.
57	 - **Metric** shows one number and nothing else: the score, the unit, a clock, the last result, the leader, or a counter or resource the pack keeps.
58	 
59	 On a Stream Deck +, Do the next thing and Metric sit on a dial as well as a key. Turning a Metric dial steps through the score, the unit, the clock, the last result and the leader, and a running clock redraws every second.
